+\section{Spiking-Mirror Implementation, Calibration, and Verification}\label{app:spiking_details}
+
+This appendix documents the numeric details behind the spiking-neuron mirrors of Section~\ref{sec:spiking_methods}, in the same file-traceable form as Appendix~\ref{app:muscle_calcs}: the cell and synapse equations as implemented, the calibration factors of record, the full verification-gate table of the MuJoCo mirror, and the variant-by-variant AnimatLab conversion table. The campaign's artifacts live under \texttt{Code/MuJoCo\_SNS/spinal/reports\_spiking\_20261002/} (reports, gate scripts, logs, and metric files) and \texttt{Code/MuJoCo\_SNS/spinal/} (the mirror builder \texttt{build\_network\_spiking.py} and its calibration script \texttt{calibrate\_spiking.py}); the Simulink blocks are built by \texttt{Code/Matlab/SNS\_Simscape/sns\_build\_spiking.m} and tested by \texttt{sns\_units\_test\_spiking.m} in the same folder.
+
+\subsection{Adapting Integrate-and-Fire Cells and Hybrid Synapses}
+
+Between spikes, every spiking cell of the MuJoCo mirror obeys the membrane equation
+\begin{equation}
+    C_{m}\,\dot{V} \;=\; -\,g_{m}\left(V - V_{\text{rest}}\right)
+        \;+\; I_{\text{syn}} \;+\; I_{\text{bias}},
+    \label{eq:app_lif}
+\end{equation}
+with a spike emitted when $V$ reaches the firing threshold $\theta$, after which $V$ resets to $V_{\text{reset}}$ and $\theta$ increases by the increment $\Delta\theta$; between spikes $\theta$ decays back toward its initial value with time constant $\tau_{\theta}$, bounded by the adaptation floor. The tonic bias $I_{\text{bias}}$ parks the equilibrium a few millivolts below threshold, reproducing the analog cells' near-threshold operating point. Table~\ref{tab:app_spk_cells} lists the per-class values as coded (SNS-Toolbox's \texttt{SpikingNeuron} class; the toolbox's membrane update is dimensionally consistent only at $g_{m} = \qty{1}{\micro\siemens}$, which the mirror therefore uses throughout). The rhythm-generator adaptation time constant reuses the analog network's persistent-sodium inactivation value, so that tuned adaptation values transfer between builds; at the rhythm gate's operating point it is \qty{0.35}{\second}.
+
+\begin{table}[htbp]
+\caption{Spiking cell parameters of the MuJoCo mirror (real millivolts; \texttt{build\_network\_spiking.py}, \texttt{SPIKE} table, with the rhythm-generator increment superseded by the calibration of record). All cells rest at \qty{-70}{\mV} with membrane conductance \qty{1}{\micro\siemens} and the tonic bias of Table~\ref{tab:app_spk_cal}.}
+\label{tab:app_spk_cells}
+\begin{tabular}{@{}lllll@{}}
+\toprule
+\textbf{Cell class} & $\boldsymbol{\theta}$ \textbf{(mV)} & $\boldsymbol{V_{\text{reset}}}$ \textbf{(mV)} & $\boldsymbol{\Delta\theta}$ \textbf{(mV/spike)} & $\boldsymbol{\tau_{\theta}}$ \textbf{(s)} \\
+\midrule
+Rhythm generator E/F & $-50$ & $-60$ & 4.0 (calibrated) & 0.35 (analog value) \\
+Pattern-formation     & $-50$ & $-60$ & 0.3 & 0.15 \\
+Interneurons, commissurals & $-50$ & $-60$ & --- & --- \\
+Afferent encoders     & $-52$ & $-58$ & --- & --- \\
